WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.853 --> 00:00:16.117
Families can bring out the best in us, and they can bring out the worst, as we see

2
00:00:16.197 --> 00:00:17.718
in the story of King Lear.

3
00:00:18.879 --> 00:00:24.623
The proud, old king does not realize his actions will cause loyalty and love to battle greed and

4
00:00:24.683 --> 00:00:26.545
hate—with tragic consequences.

5
00:00:27.105 --> 00:00:29.547
The story begins in the great hall of his castle.

6
00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:34.562
Lear, king of England, had grown tired of his responsibilities.

7
00:00:34.582 --> 00:00:41.565
"It is time," he announced, "to pass on my duties to those who are younger, while I, free

8
00:00:41.585 --> 00:00:43.727
of my burden, crawl toward death.

9
00:00:44.987 --> 00:00:49.350
I shall divide my kingdom into three parts, one for each of my daughters."

10
00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:52.191
Lear then unrolled a map.

11
00:00:52.211 --> 00:00:57.594
"I will give the biggest part," he said, "to the one who convinces me she loves me most."

12
00:00:58.795 --> 00:01:04.130
He turned to his oldest daughter, Goneril, who stood beside her husband, the Duke of Albany.

13
00:01:04.771 --> 00:01:06.752
"Speak first," Lear commanded.

14
00:01:08.213 --> 00:01:14.918
Goneril said, "I love you more than words can say, Father, beyond anything that can be measured, and

15
00:01:14.978 --> 00:01:17.380
as much as freedom and life itself."

16
00:01:18.881 --> 00:01:23.084
Smiling insincerely, she went on with more pretty phrases.

17
00:01:24.365 --> 00:01:27.528
Cordelia, Lear's youngest daughter, listened with disgust.

18
00:01:28.072 --> 00:01:31.893
She knew her sister would say anything to get as much land as possible.

19
00:01:33.073 --> 00:01:35.754
But Lear was very pleased by his oldest daughter's words.

20
00:01:36.334 --> 00:01:37.935
He pointed to a section on the map.

21
00:01:37.955 --> 00:01:42.576
"From here to here, all this will be yours and Albany's.

22
00:01:43.776 --> 00:01:49.178
Now, what says my second daughter, Regan, dear wife of the Duke of Cornwall?"

23
00:01:50.398 --> 00:01:51.858
Regan boldly stepped forward.

24
00:01:51.878 --> 00:01:57.580
"My sister's words also describe my love for you, except she hasn't gone far enough.

25
00:01:58.916 --> 00:02:02.257
Nothing in life gives me joy except my love for you!"

26
00:02:02.737 --> 00:02:03.897
she cried dramatically.

27
00:02:05.298 --> 00:02:06.838
Cordelia was now very upset.

28
00:02:07.238 --> 00:02:09.099
"How can I compete with these lies?"

29
00:02:09.399 --> 00:02:09.779
she thought.

30
00:02:09.799 --> 00:02:14.840
"Yet, I know my love for my father is greater than I can express."

31
00:02:16.021 --> 00:02:20.422
But again, Lear was delighted, and indicated another part of the map.

32
00:02:20.442 --> 00:02:26.804
"This is for you and Cornwall," he said to Regan, "and it is equal to Goneril's share."

33
00:02:27.904 --> 00:02:29.625
Then he turned to Cordelia.

34
00:02:29.645 --> 00:02:36.270
"And you, my youngest and my joy, what can you say to win the remaining third, the finest

35
00:02:36.310 --> 00:02:37.090
part of my kingdom?

36
00:02:37.631 --> 00:02:41.674
Speak!" "Nothing, my lord," replied Cordelia quietly.

37
00:02:42.834 --> 00:02:44.696
"Nothing?" said Lear, shocked.

38
00:02:45.256 --> 00:02:46.597
"Nothing will come of nothing.

39
00:02:47.177 --> 00:02:47.738
Speak again."

40
00:02:48.959 --> 00:02:49.999
Cordelia looked down.

41
00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:53.642
She did not want to use flattery, as her sisters had done.

42
00:02:53.662 --> 00:03:00.118
"Dear Father," she said, "I love you as a child should—no more, no less."

43
00:03:01.399 --> 00:03:02.700
Lear was angry now.

44
00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:05.922
"Explain yourself, or you may live to regret it!"

45
00:03:07.343 --> 00:03:12.487
"Sir, I obey, love, and honor you as a daughter should," answered Cordelia.

46
00:03:12.507 --> 00:03:16.989
"Why do my sisters have husbands if they say they love you only?

47
00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:22.393
If I marry, it's only fair that my husband take half my love with him."

48
00:03:23.114 --> 00:03:25.075
"So young and so hard-hearted?"

49
00:03:25.355 --> 00:03:26.556
said her father, stunned.

50
00:03:27.748 --> 00:03:30.250
"So young and true, my lord," replied Cordelia.

51
00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:34.373
"Then let truth be your dowry," raged Lear.

52
00:03:34.853 --> 00:03:36.114
"You are no longer my daughter.

53
00:03:37.315 --> 00:03:42.058
I looked forward to your care and affection in my old age, but now I disown you!"

54
00:03:43.219 --> 00:03:46.522
Cordelia stared at her father, devastated by his words.

55
00:03:46.542 --> 00:03:53.327
"Your share of the kingdom," the king went on, "will be divided between your sisters and their husbands."

56
00:03:53.987 --> 00:03:58.301
Lear took off his crown and motioned to Albany and Cornwall to step forward.

57
00:03:58.321 --> 00:04:04.304
"Take this, for you are now my sons and will rule the land together."

58
00:04:05.404 --> 00:04:11.466
To Goneril and Regan, he said, "All that is mine is now yours, except for one hundred knights,

59
00:04:12.027 --> 00:04:13.987
whom I shall keep to attend to me.

60
00:04:15.128 --> 00:04:18.389
And I shall come live with each of you in turn for one month at a time."

61
00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:24.252
At that moment, the Earl of Kent, Lear's most loyal nobleman, stepped forward.

62
00:04:24.272 --> 00:04:27.425
"My lord," he said, "you're behaving rashly.

63
00:04:28.525 --> 00:04:31.286
Your youngest daughter certainly does not love you least.

64
00:04:31.866 --> 00:04:33.806
I beg you, reconsider your decision."

65
00:04:33.826 --> 00:04:37.127
"Do not come between the dragon and his wrath!"

66
00:04:37.487 --> 00:04:37.967
cried Lear.

67
00:04:37.987 --> 00:04:39.748
"How dare you?

68
00:04:40.348 --> 00:04:43.809
I have spoken, and yet, you want me to go back on my word?

69
00:04:45.009 --> 00:04:46.290
You are banished, Kent!

70
00:04:46.810 --> 00:04:50.551
If you are found in England ten days from now, you will be put to death!"

71
00:04:51.811 --> 00:04:52.791
Kent bowed his head.

72
00:04:52.811 --> 00:04:54.652
"Then fare thee well, my lord."

73
00:04:55.148 --> 00:05:00.190
To Cordelia, he said, "May the gods look after you—you spoke fairly and truthfully."

74
00:05:01.591 --> 00:05:03.211
He turned to Goneril and Regan.

75
00:05:03.671 --> 00:05:06.533
"And I hope your deeds will match your fancy speeches."

76
00:05:07.173 --> 00:05:09.834
Bidding everyone good-bye, Kent left the castle.

77
00:05:11.054 --> 00:05:13.395
There was one more matter to be resolved that day.

78
00:05:13.936 --> 00:05:19.998
Cordelia, the only daughter who wasn't married, had two suitors at court: the Duke of Burgundy and the

79
00:05:20.038 --> 00:05:20.738
king of France.

80
00:05:21.338 --> 00:05:22.419
Lear called them in.

81
00:05:23.579 --> 00:05:26.445
"Lord Burgundy," he said, "do you still want my daughter?

82
00:05:26.986 --> 00:05:29.147
She has lost my love and her dowry."

83
00:05:29.167 --> 00:05:33.571
"Give her back the lands you promised her, and I'll marry her," replied the duke.

84
00:05:34.712 --> 00:05:36.334
But Lear would not change his mind.

85
00:05:36.354 --> 00:05:39.777
"Then I am sorry," said the duke to Cordelia.

86
00:05:39.797 --> 00:05:43.660
"Having lost a father, you must also lose a husband."

87
00:05:44.841 --> 00:05:47.904
"What has she done that you would disown your most beloved daughter?"

88
00:05:48.364 --> 00:05:49.365
the king of France asked.

89
00:05:50.826 --> 00:05:51.627
Cordelia spoke.

90
00:05:53.044 --> 00:05:57.488
"Sir, my offense was simply that I would rather show my love to my father than speak of

91
00:05:57.568 --> 00:05:59.249
it." "Is that all?"

92
00:05:59.689 --> 00:06:00.470
said the king of France.

93
00:06:01.031 --> 00:06:05.714
He truly loved Cordelia; he did not care that she had lost her third of the kingdom.

94
00:06:05.734 --> 00:06:10.398
"Come with me to France, Cordelia," he said gently, "and be my queen."

95
00:06:11.519 --> 00:06:13.440
Cordelia turned to Goneril and Regan.

96
00:06:13.460 --> 00:06:17.183
"You are my sisters, so I do not want to speak badly of you.

97
00:06:18.464 --> 00:06:22.568
But knowing you both the way I do, I fear for my father's welfare.

98
00:06:23.192 --> 00:06:25.034
Still, try to love him well."

99
00:06:26.154 --> 00:06:29.157
"Don't tell us our duty," Goneril snapped back.

100
00:06:30.297 --> 00:06:32.479
The king of France then took Cordelia's arm.

101
00:06:32.499 --> 00:06:33.680
"Come, dearest.

102
00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:35.902
We shall leave for France tonight."

103
00:06:36.422 --> 00:06:37.623
And they left the great hall.

104
00:06:38.804 --> 00:06:40.245
Goneril drew Regan aside.

105
00:06:40.265 --> 00:06:45.689
"Sister," she whispered, "I think our father will be coming to stay with me tonight.

106
00:06:46.229 --> 00:06:47.730
So you and I need to talk now.

107
00:06:48.191 --> 00:06:49.692
You see how strange he's acting?

108
00:06:51.168 --> 00:06:54.490
He always loved our sister the most, and now he's rejected her.

109
00:06:55.111 --> 00:06:56.552
And he banished Kent too!

110
00:06:57.132 --> 00:06:58.193
It must be his age.

111
00:06:58.733 --> 00:07:00.254
He's going to be nothing but trouble."

112
00:07:00.274 --> 00:07:05.438
"And it's only going to get worse as he grows older," muttered Regan.

113
00:07:05.458 --> 00:07:08.960
"We must do something about him," her sister said.

114
00:07:08.980 --> 00:07:10.961
"And we must act fast."

115
00:07:12.222 --> 00:07:18.386
Also present in the great hall was Edmund, a handsome young man who had watched Lear disinherit Cordelia.

116
00:07:18.906 --> 00:07:20.908
Her situation reminded him of his own.

117
00:07:22.312 --> 00:07:28.596
Edmund was the younger—and illegitimate—son of the Earl of Gloucester, a trusted friend of Lear.

118
00:07:29.116 --> 00:07:32.518
The earl had an older son, Edgar, who was his legal heir.

119
00:07:32.538 --> 00:07:38.341
"The law says I shall never inherit anything from my father either," thought Edmund.

120
00:07:38.361 --> 00:07:39.641
"That is not fair.

121
00:07:40.222 --> 00:07:42.543
I'm just as brave and clever as my brother.

122
00:07:43.764 --> 00:07:45.745
In fact, I'm more clever.

123
00:07:46.265 --> 00:07:52.193
Because I have a plan to become my father's only son and heir—I shall get rid of Edgar!"
